{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91560d1c43ece6cb","type":"tool_result","content":"# MaskGCT: Zero-Shot Text-to-Speech with Masked Generative Codec Transformer\narXiv: 2409.00750\nAuthors: Yuancheng Wang, Haoyue Zhan, Liwei Liu, Ruihong Zeng, Haotian Guo, Jiachen Zheng, Qiang Zhang, Xueyao Zhang, Shunsi Zhang, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Proposes MaskGCT, a fully non-autogressive text-to-speech system that eliminates the need for explicit text-speech alignment supervision and phone-level duration prediction.\n  2. Introduces a two-stage masked generative transformer framework consisting of a text-to-semantic model and a semantic-to-acoustic model.\n  3. Trains a VQ-VAE on speech self-supervised learning representations to extract discrete semantic tokens, minimizing information loss compared to traditional k-means quantization.\n  4. Achieves human-level or state-of-the-art performance in zero-shot TTS regarding speech quality, similarity, and intelligibility on multiple benchmarks.\n  5. Demonstrates scalability to diverse speech generation tasks, including cross-lingual dubbing, emotion control, speech content editing, and voice conversion.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多说话人, TTS/功能-语音编辑","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee312e58-0c88-4e9f-ad8c-2c50c5143559","uuid":"71c74702-5ebc-40a5-ace1-3c4aafcb9e5a","timestamp":"2026-08-12T10:50:05.048Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# MaskGCT: Zero-Shot Text-to-Speech with Masked Generative Codec Transformer\narXiv: 2409.00750\nAuthors: Yuancheng Wang, Haoyue Zhan, Liwei Liu, Ruihong Zeng, Haotian Guo, Jiachen Zheng, Qiang Zhang, Xueyao Zhang, Shunsi Zhang, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Proposes MaskGCT, a fully non-autogressive text-to-speech system that eliminates the need for explicit text-speech alignment supervision and phone-level duration prediction.\n  2. Introduces a two-stage masked generative transformer framework consisting of a text-to-semantic model and a semantic-to-acoustic model.\n  3. Trains a VQ-VAE on speech self-supervised learning representations to extract discrete semantic tokens, minimizing information loss compared to traditional k-means quantization.\n  4. Achieves human-level or state-of-the-art performance in zero-shot TTS regarding speech quality, similarity, and intelligibility on multiple benchmarks.\n  5. Demonstrates scalability to diverse speech generation tasks, including cross-lingual dubbing, emotion control, speech content editing, and voice conversion.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多说话人, TTS/功能-语音编辑","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
